1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,440
Welcome back everyone.

2
00:00:01,790 --> 00:00:05,870
Today I'm joined once again by Eve from Club Madeira.

3
00:00:06,220 --> 00:00:08,092
Eve, thank you for being here.

4
00:00:09,042 --> 00:00:10,410
Always a pleasure, Leo.

5
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:22,856
So, if I wanted to become a partner — say I'm a website designer or digital agency working with clubs — walk me through what that would look like, especially the white-label side.

6
00:00:23,806 --> 00:00:26,086
That's the part partners love most.

7
00:00:26,436 --> 00:00:31,116
The Smart Catalogue is built from the ground up as a fully white-label product.

8
00:00:31,466 --> 00:00:34,226
Clubs never see Club Madeira branding.

9
00:00:34,576 --> 00:00:42,400
When you embed it, the entire experience appears under your client's brand, on their domain, with their colours, logo and voice.

10
00:00:42,750 --> 00:00:48,006
From the member's point of view it simply feels like the club's own professional online shop.

11
00:00:48,356 --> 00:00:51,020
That's a huge selling point for agencies.

12
00:00:51,970 --> 00:00:55,066
So I control the look and feel completely?

13
00:00:56,016 --> 00:00:57,048
Completely.

14
00:00:57,398 --> 00:01:04,646
You control the branding, the pricing you charge the club, the level of support you offer, and the ongoing client relationship.

15
00:01:04,996 --> 00:01:06,532
We stay in the background.

16
00:01:06,882 --> 00:01:15,522
You deliver a white-labelled Progressive Web App experience that members can even install on their phones — still fully branded as the club.

17
00:01:16,472 --> 00:01:19,568
Can I modify the code myself if I need to?

18
00:01:20,518 --> 00:01:21,238
Yes.

19
00:01:21,588 --> 00:01:27,300
The complete partner integration code is available under the MIT open-source licence.

20
00:01:27,650 --> 00:01:31,370
You're free to use it, modify it, and extend it however you need.

21
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:40,600
That means you can adapt the widgets, adjust the PWA behaviour, or build additional features on top without asking permission or paying extra.

22
00:01:40,950 --> 00:01:45,870
It's designed so agencies can properly own the technical delivery for their clients.

23
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:52,724
That makes it feel like a premium service I'm providing, not a locked-down third-party tool.

24
00:01:53,674 --> 00:01:54,586
Exactly.

25
00:01:54,936 --> 00:01:57,312
You're not reselling someone else's platform.

26
00:01:57,662 --> 00:02:03,302
You're embedding a powerful fundraising engine that becomes part of the club's own digital presence.

27
00:02:03,652 --> 00:02:10,396
And because it's white-label and open source under MIT, you can position and customise it however you like.

28
00:02:11,346 --> 00:02:14,250
How does the commercial side work in that model?

29
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:22,304
When members shop, the club earns commission, you earn recurring revenue, and merchants get targeted exposure.

30
00:02:22,654 --> 00:02:24,766
There are no monthly platform fees.

31
00:02:25,116 --> 00:02:31,116
Your technical work is the clean integration, branding, and any modifications you choose to make.

32
00:02:31,466 --> 00:02:34,946
The ongoing commercial opportunity is driving engagement.

33
00:02:35,296 --> 00:02:39,976
We expect each active catalogue to generate around two thousand clicks a month.

34
00:02:40,326 --> 00:02:46,182
That comes from the marketing, SEO and promotion that you bill the club for as a paid service.

35
00:02:47,132 --> 00:02:55,364
So the white-label nature plus the MIT licence lets me own the whole relationship and charge properly for the value.

36
00:02:56,314 --> 00:02:57,298
That's the model.

37
00:02:57,648 --> 00:03:01,248
You bring the clubs, the websites and the promotional expertise.

38
00:03:01,598 --> 00:03:07,286
We provide the AI, the product vault and the infrastructure — all invisible to the end user.

39
00:03:07,636 --> 00:03:12,772
It turns a simple website add-on into a high-value, recurring service under your brand.

40
00:03:13,722 --> 00:03:15,138
That's very clear.

41
00:03:15,488 --> 00:03:18,656
What's the practical first step if I wanted to start?

42
00:03:19,606 --> 00:03:32,734
You become an approved partner, receive your affiliate code and the full partner package — including the MIT-licensed integration code — then begin embedding the white-label catalogue for your existing club clients.

43
00:03:33,084 --> 00:03:36,780
From day one it looks and feels like something you built for them.

44
00:03:37,730 --> 00:03:38,810
Thank you, Eve.

45
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:40,888
That's extremely helpful.

46
00:03:41,838 --> 00:03:42,870
Thank you, Leo.

47
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:45,092
Happy to go deeper any time.

